-- title:
--   At most h symmetric 2-cocycles span the rigidified ones
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $F_0$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$, i.e. an $n$-tuple of power series $F_0(X,Y)$ in the two blocks of variables indexed by `Fin n ⊕ Fin n` with vanishing constant terms, linear parts $X_i + Y_i$, and the associativity identity $F_0(F_0(X,Y),Z)=F_0(X,F_0(Y,Z))$, assumed commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks fixes each component. Write $[m]_{F_0}$ for the $m$-th iterate `nthSeries`, defined by $[0]_{F_0}=0$ and $[m+1]_{F_0}=F_0([m]_{F_0}(X),X)$. Assume that for some $h \in \mathbb{N}$ the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ by the ideal generated by the $n$ components of $[p]_{F_0}$ has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Then there are an $s \le h$, power series $\Gamma_1,\dots,\Gamma_s$ in the $2n$ variables and vectors $c_1,\dots,c_s \in k^n$ such that each $\Gamma_j$ is a symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle for $F_0$ (constant term $0$, invariant under interchanging the two blocks of variables, and $\Gamma_j(F_0(X,Y),Z)+\Gamma_j(X,Y)=\Gamma_j(X,F_0(Y,Z))+\Gamma_j(Y,Z)$), and such that for every symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle $\Gamma'$ for $F_0$ and every vector $c' \in k^n$ there exist scalars $a_1,\dots,a_s \in k$ and a power series $g$ in $X_1,\dots,X_n$ with $g(0)=0$ satisfying $\Gamma' = \sum_j a_j \Gamma_j + \big(g(F_0(X,Y))-g(X)-g(Y)\big)$ and, for each $l$, $c'_l = \sum_j a_j (c_j)_l + \mathrm{coeff}_{X_l}(g)$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$p$ inequality underlying the theorem of Mazur–Messing and Katz that the rigidified extensions of a formal group of height $h$ by $\mathbb{G}_a$ form a module of rank $h$: the $k$-vector space of pairs $(\Gamma,c)$ consisting of a symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle and a linear form on the tangent space, modulo the coboundaries $(\partial g, \mathrm{d}g(0))$ coming from coordinate changes $u \mapsto u + g(X)$, is spanned by at most $h$ classes. It feeds the companion statement [`MvFormalGroup.exists_isSymmTwoCocycle_span_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_isSymmTwoCocycle_span_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow), in which the rigidifying vectors are dropped.
